WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.281
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online IELTS preparation.

2
00:00:05.581 --> 00:00:09.129
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:17.179
Unit twenty: Speaking Part 3 and Full Mock Review. Today you will discuss abstract ideas in depth and review the whole test strategy.

4
00:00:17.479 --> 00:00:20.421
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:24.541
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.383 --> 00:00:26.477
Abstract.

7
00:00:27.483 --> 00:00:30.853
Abstract means about ideas, not physical things.

8
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.879
Part 3 uses abstract questions.

9
00:00:34.483 --> 00:00:37.136
Your turn. Say: Abstract.

10
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.094
Abstract.

11
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:42.967
Justify.

12
00:00:43.983 --> 00:00:46.529
Justify means to give reasons for an opinion.

13
00:00:47.117 --> 00:00:48.559
Justify your view.

14
00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.814
Your turn. Say: Justify.

15
00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:55.935
Justify.

16
00:00:56.683 --> 00:00:57.742
Speculate.

17
00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:02.061
Speculate means to guess about the future or possibilities.

18
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:04.824
Speculate about future changes.

19
00:01:05.417 --> 00:01:08.104
Your turn. Say: Speculate.

20
00:01:10.967 --> 00:01:12.142
Speculate.

21
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:13.815
Compare.

22
00:01:14.817 --> 00:01:17.838
Compare means to show similarities and differences.

23
00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:20.751
Compare life now and in the past.

24
00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:23.410
Your turn. Say: Compare.

25
00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:27.186
Compare.

26
00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:28.742
Trend.

27
00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.446
Trend means a general direction of change.

28
00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:35.282
A growing trend is online study.

29
00:01:35.883 --> 00:01:38.025
Your turn. Say: Trend.

30
00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:41.670
Trend.

31
00:01:42.417 --> 00:01:43.557
It depends.

32
00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:47.397
It depends means used when the answer is not simple.

33
00:01:47.983 --> 00:01:49.530
It depends on the person.

34
00:01:50.117 --> 00:01:52.815
Your turn. Say: It depends.

35
00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:56.888
It depends.

36
00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:58.837
Mock test.

37
00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:02.976
Mock test means a practice test like the real one.

38
00:02:03.583 --> 00:02:05.235
Take a full mock test.

39
00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.862
Your turn. Say: Mock test.

40
00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:12.748
Mock test.

41
00:02:13.483 --> 00:02:14.357
Feedback.

42
00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:17.976
Feedback means advice that helps you improve.

43
00:02:18.583 --> 00:02:20.455
Ask your teacher for feedback.

44
00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:23.575
Your turn. Say: Feedback.

45
00:02:26.433 --> 00:02:27.225
Feedback.

46
00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:31.440
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:32.283 --> 00:02:35.072
Visal, how is Part 3 different from Part 2?

48
00:02:36.183 --> 00:02:47.578
Part 3 is a longer discussion linked to the Part 2 topic. The questions are more abstract, such as how travel has changed or what governments should do.

49
00:02:48.683 --> 00:02:50.520
How do I give a strong answer?

50
00:02:51.617 --> 00:03:03.174
State your view, justify it with a reason, and give an example. You can also compare the past and the present, or speculate about the future, using phrases like it depends and I would say.

51
00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:06.411
How can I prepare for the whole test?

52
00:03:07.517 --> 00:03:19.294
Take full mock tests under timed conditions and review each module. Ask for feedback, correct your mistakes, and repeat your weak areas every week.

53
00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:22.131
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:22.983 --> 00:03:27.363
Grammar focus: Strategy: justify, compare, speculate.

55
00:03:27.663 --> 00:03:28.954
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:33.054
I would say that online study is growing because it is flexible.

57
00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:37.215
It depends on the person, but most students enjoy it.

58
00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:47.506
In Part 3, give your view, explain why, and add an example. Use compare and speculate language, and review all four modules with timed mock tests.

59
00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:52.307
Be careful! Don't say: I only practise my strongest skill.

60
00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:57.160
Say: I practise my weakest area weekly.

61
00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:58.937
Work on weak areas.

62
00:03:59.733 --> 00:04:02.270
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:04.439
Discussing Change.

64
00:04:04.739 --> 00:04:07.888
The examiner asks how travel has changed over time.

65
00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:12.153
Rithy says that travel is faster and cheaper than before.

66
00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:16.931
He justifies this with the growth of low-cost flights and online booking.

67
00:04:17.933 --> 00:04:21.570
He speculates that more people will travel for study in the future.

68
00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:25.948
He ends by saying it depends on each country's policies.

69
00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:31.267
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:32.117 --> 00:04:34.302
Part 3 questions are usually blank.

71
00:04:34.602 --> 00:04:38.998
A, about maps. B, one word. C, abstract.

72
00:04:42.533 --> 00:04:44.858
The answer is C: abstract.

73
00:04:46.017 --> 00:04:47.494
To justify is to blank.

74
00:04:47.794 --> 00:04:52.643
A, give reasons. B, stop speaking. C, spell.

75
00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.629
The answer is A: give reasons.

76
00:04:59.783 --> 00:05:01.620
'It depends' is used when blank.

77
00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:07.002
A, you finish. B, the answer is not simple. C, you do not speak.

78
00:05:10.567 --> 00:05:13.414
The answer is B: the answer is not simple.

79
00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:16.840
How should you prepare for the whole test?

80
00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:21.768
A, only reading. B, skip Speaking. C, timed mock tests.

81
00:05:25.333 --> 00:05:28.331
The answer is C: timed mock tests.

82
00:05:29.483 --> 00:05:31.169
What does Rithy speculate?

83
00:05:31.469 --> 00:05:37.004
A, more people will travel for study. B, travel will stop. C, flights will disappear.

84
00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:44.134
The answer is A: more people will travel for study.

85
00:05:45.333 --> 00:05:48.218
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:49.083 --> 00:05:51.547
How do you prepare for the whole IELTS test?

87
00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:01.839
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:06:02.139 --> 00:06:18.354
I take timed mock tests for all four modules and review my mistakes with a teacher. I practise Speaking by giving reasons and examples, and I practise Writing with a plan. Every week I repeat my weakest area until it improves.

89
00:06:18.654 --> 00:06:20.433
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:21.317 --> 00:06:27.301
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: justify, compare, speculate.

91
00:06:27.601 --> 00:06:32.111
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

92
00:06:32.411 --> 00:06:39.246
Congratulations! You have finished Online IELTS preparation. See you in Online TOEFL preparation!

93
00:06:39.546 --> 00:06:42.140
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

